 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Zero Alpha:** If `OUT.a` is 0, the lighting calculation is skipped, and `OUT` remains white `(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0)` with alpha 0. If alpha blending is used without proper alpha testing or if the background is not black, this results in white fragments being blended into the image [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Normal Interpretation:** The method assumes the RGB components of the volume data represent surface normals. If the volume data represents scalar density, this approach will produce incorrect lighting unless the RGB channels are explicitly pre-computed as normals [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Light Position Usage:** The diffuse term uses `lightPosition` directly in the dot product instead of the normalized light direction vector $\mathbf{L}$. This is a specific implementation detail of the cited source and deviates from the standard Phong model definition [S2, unofficial].
