 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Performance:** The technique using fragment shaders (Cg) results in lower performance compared to using the fixed-function pipeline of OpenGL [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Texture Orientation:** 3D textures oriented to the view plane have substantially lower performance than those oriented to the object plane [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Texture Access:** 3D texture accesses are slower than 2D texture accesses due to irregular memory access patterns [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Alpha Testing:** Enabling alpha test generates more frames per second compared to disabling it [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Zoom Effect:** The performance of polygons oriented to the projection plane improves when the zoom increases [S2, unofficial].
